WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.732 --> 00:00:02.420
SPEAKER 1: Here at
Whirlpool, we're

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.970
the largest manufacturer
of appliances in the world.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:10.190
SPEAKER 2: Whirlpool has
been around almost 104 years.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.230
It started right here in
Benton Harbor, Michigan.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:17.100
We have 100,000
employees now worldwide.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.410
SPEAKER 3: We're a very
relationship-based company.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.532
We kind of have
small town values.

00:00:21.532 --> 00:00:23.240
The center of everything
is the customer,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.285
because that's where
our responsibility lies.

00:00:25.285 --> 00:00:26.910
SPEAKER 1: Coming to
work at Whirlpool,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.826
you get to work with
some really great people.

00:00:28.826 --> 00:00:31.556
And you get to be a part of
products that are exciting.

00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:33.180
Being able to execute
our business well

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.310
requires collaboration between
sales and merchandising teams,

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:39.367
between our manufacturing,
our product teams.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.950
SPEAKER 2: The need
that we have to be

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.210
connected, the
speed with which we

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.150
need to operate have gone up.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.170
SPEAKER 4: The opportunity
to make a global company

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:54.240
feel local, entrepreneurial,
feel fast-paced,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.010
that's a big challenge.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.460
Google Apps helps us get there.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.810
What we've really done is
create an opportunity for people

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:05.370
to collaborate truly on a
global basis, regardless

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.900
of location, time, and place.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.700
And that makes a huge
difference in terms

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.799
of the speed at
which we can operate.

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:13.340
SPEAKER 1: We're
tracking our metrics

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.042
all in one place
for the entire team.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.500
We're looking at
it and saying, how

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.666
are we going to be able to
deliver our products when

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:21.019
our customers need it.

00:01:21.019 --> 00:01:22.560
SPEAKER 4: The tools
really do create

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.920
that kind of
empowerment, to turn

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.566
people loose to be creative
and be their best self at work.

00:01:28.566 --> 00:01:30.860
SPEAKER 1: We're really
creating products

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.700
that can make families'
lives a little bit better

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.346
in a behind-the-scenes
kind of way.

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:37.720
When we think
about our customer,

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.820
we try to think about
the way that they

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.210
would want to spend
their lives, and how

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.870
we can make that better.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.620
[MUSIC PLAYING]

